<%#
  A report: a date-range filter above one card of results.

  Locals: filter_url, title, subtitle (optional), footer (optional), id (optional), actions
  (optional, for the page header), and `padded: false` when the body is a table that should meet
  the card's edges.

  Every report using this had **no way back to the reports hub** -- no breadcrumb, no back link,
  and none of them is in the sidebar, so the only route out was the browser button. The trail is
  set here rather than at each call site because it is the same trail for all of them.

  Callers used to pass `gradient:`, `footer_options:` and `type:` as well. This partial has
  never read any of them -- they are AdminLTE vocabulary that outlived the markup -- so they
  have been removed from the call sites rather than left to imply the partial does something
  with them.
%>
<%
  id ||= nil
  title ||= nil
  subtitle ||= nil
  footer ||= nil
  padded = true if defined?(padded).nil? || padded.nil?
%>
<div class="px-4 py-6 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <%#
    `actions:` is the page header's, not the card's. The manufacturer report had a "New donation"
    button between its list and its footer, which is where a form's submit goes rather than a page
    action -- and it was the only report with one, so there was nowhere to put it until now.
  %>
  <%= render "shared/essentials/page_header", title: title, subtitle: subtitle,
        actions: local_assigns[:actions],
        back: {path: reports_path, label: "Back to reports"} %>

  <%#
    The shared filter bar rather than a hand-rolled form, so a report's date filter behaves like
    every other filter in the app: applied on change, into the frame below, with no button.
  %>
  <%= render "shared/essentials/filter_bar", url: filter_url, frame: "report-results" do %>
    <div class="min-w-0"><%= render partial: "shared/date_range_picker" %></div>
  <% end %>

  <%= turbo_frame_tag "report-results", target: "_top", data: {turbo_action: "advance"} do %>
    <%= render "shared/essentials/card", footer: footer, padded: padded do %>
      <div<%= " id=#{id.to_json.html_safe}".html_safe if id %>>
        <%= yield %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
